BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dungeons & Dragons Group A
DTSTART:20260809T121500
DTEND:20260809T151500
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:faff225b0f03592d28d637994796c7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:D&amp\;D is back with your favorite Dungeon Master\, Andrew\, 
 now in two smaller groups with capped registration! "Group A" will play on
  the second Sunday of each month\, and "Group B" will play on the third Su
 nday of each month. Pre-registration required\, a waitlist will be availab
 le if we fill up. Please choose only one Group each month.<br/><br/>For al
 l experience levels\, ages 9-14\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kids & Family
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/dungeons-a
 mp-dragons-group-a-05-08-2026-09-32-22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Food for Talk Cookbook Club
DTSTART:20260809T150000
DTEND:20260809T170000
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:c6f520c1a7aedb46533febb938798c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Food for Talk is a book club for anyone interested in cooking!
  Instructions on how to join this community of home cooks and fellow culin
 ary travelers can be found after the description of this month's cookbook.
  If reading about food\, experimenting with new recipes and learning from 
 other cooks sounds fun\, sign up and join us on the second Sunday of every
  month at 3pm! Locations vary.<br/><br/>This month: Portugal: Recipes and 
 Ingredients by Anais Delon<br/><br/>Please register with Barbara Shatara a
 t bshatara@burlingtonvt.gov\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Food & Drink
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/food-for-t
 alk-cookbook-club-05-08-2026-09-34-25
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury: House of Hamill
DTSTART:20260809T170000
DTEND:20260809T190000
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:1b0053f57bd61b05e785a59842efa8@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Catamount Arts welcomes Celtic folk group House of Hamill to D
 og Mountain\, Sunday\, August 9th\, as part of the Levitt AMP St. Johnsbur
 y Music Series. The Philadelphia trio takes the stage at 5pm\, for a rousi
 ng set of jigs\, reels\, and lush three-part harmonies.<br/>House of Hamil
 l began at a Folk Alliance International conference when Rose Baldino\, wh
 ose bandmates were stranded in an airport\, recruited Brian Buchanan\, of 
 Enter the Haggis\, to join her onstage. Years later\, Caroline Browning an
 swered a frantic Facebook post when\, once again\, Baldino and Buchanan ne
 eded a bass player at the last minute. The rest is history.<br/><br/>Today
 \, Pennsylvania-based House of Hamill is a festival fixture\, sharing thei
 r music and stories on premier folk stages all over the country. Their ori
 ginal song “Banks of the Brandywine” was a 2024 John Lennon Songwritin
 g Contest Grand Prize winner\, and the video for their all-violin cover of
  “Sweet Child O’ Mine” has amassed over 16 million views on Facebook
  and been shared nearly half a million times.<br/><br/>The band’s latest
  release\, “Wildfire\,” marks House of Hamill’s most compelling work
  to date. Featuring their strongest and most exciting songwriting\, “Wil
 dfire” is filled with lyrical depth\, sophisticated vocal and instrument
 al arrangements\, and hooks that are simply irresistible. This album captu
 res the vibrant energy and creativity that have become the hallmarks of a 
 House of Hamill live show.<br/><br/>Whether they’re ripping through a se
 t of original jigs and reels\, layering three-part harmonies over traditio
 nal folk ballads\, or cracking up an audience with stories from the road\,
  House of Hamill captivates audiences from the very first note.<br/>House 
 of Hamill’s concert at Dog Mountain is free and open to everyone—inclu
 ding dogs. Patrons are encouraged to bring a blanket or a low beach chair\
 , sunscreen\, and water\, but leave the alcohol at home. Beer\, wine\, and
  cocktails will be available for purchase at the St. Johnsbury Distillery 
 beer garden on site\; bringing alcohol from off-site is strictly prohibite
 d. Patrons are welcome to pack a picnic dinner or bring cash to grab somet
 hing from one of the food trucks\; there will be at least two food options
  available for purchase at every Sunday concert.<br/>Overflow parking is a
 vailable at the Fairbanks Scales parking lot\, where RCT will shuttle pass
 engers up to Dog Mountain and back. New this year\, RCT will begin shuttli
 ng folks from the St. Johnsbury Welcome Center to Dog Mountain every Sunda
 y at 4pm\, and then back to the Welcome Center after the concert. Thanks t
 o generous support from RCT\, shuttle service to the concert venue is free
  of charge.<br/><br/>In addition to monthly Sunday concerts at Dog Mountai
 n\, Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury will host free concerts at Final Fridays bloc
 k parties\, on the last Friday of June\, July\, and August\, in partnershi
 p with Downtown St. Johnsbury. For a full summer of free family-friendly l
 ive music\, plan to be at Dog Mountain\, every Sunday\, at 5pm\, and don
 ’t miss Final Fridays on Railroad Street!<br/>For more information\, inc
 luding the full line-up of Levitt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series artists\,
  visit www.catamountarts.org or email info@catamountarts.org. <br/>To lear
 n more about Final Fridays block parties\, featuring free family-friendly 
 activities in downtown St. Johnsbury including live music courtesy of Levi
 tt AMP St. Johnsbury\, visit www.discoverstjohnsbury.org. <br/><br/>The Le
 vitt AMP St. Johnsbury Music Series is supported in part by the Levitt Fam
 ily Foundation\, which exists to strengthen the social fabric of America. 
 The Levitt Family Foundation partners with communities to activate underus
 ed outdoor spaces\, creating welcoming inclusive destinations where the po
 wer of free live music brings people together and invigorates community li
 fe. <br/><br/>In 2026\, the Levitt Family Foundation is supporting over 1\
 ,000 free concerts in 100+ towns and cities throughout the country\, bring
 ing joy to over a million people. In addition to supporting free concerts\
 , the Levitt Foundation is dedicated to advancing equitable music ecosyste
 ms through research and partnerships. Learn more at www.levitt.org. <br/>\
 n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Kids & Family
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/levitt-amp
 -st-johnsbury-house-of-hamill-17-07-2026-07-13-18
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Play Every Town Concert in Charleston VT
DTSTART:20260809T140000
DTEND:20260809T153000
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:c6283667fc41b97ad772d901cd2e3d@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Renowned pianist David Feurzeig will perform his 103rd Vermont
  concert on Sunday August 9 at 2:00 pm in Charleston VT at the Plymouth Co
 ngregational Church\, 7068 VT-105\, East Charleston\, with local performer
 s Annabelle Jensen and Mark Bechtold\, continuing David’s exciting tour-
 -a free show in all of Vermont’s 252 towns to spread the joy of music an
 d promote environmentally sustainable performance. In May of 2022\, he emb
 arked on his Play Every Town project: 252 free concerts in each of Vermont
 ’s 252 towns to combat climate change through the power of community and
  music. With this project David will become the first musician to perform 
 in every Vermont municipality. He will travel in his solar-charged electri
 c vehicle throughout the state\, offering free concerts to bring attention
  to the interrelated issues of climate and community\, while bringing the 
 joy of music to his audiences.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Music: Classical
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/play-every
 -town-concert-in-charleston-vt-27-07-2026-20-13-33
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Star Lane Sox and Scott Hsu at Stage 33 Live
DTSTART:20260809T150000
DTEND:20260809T170000
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:49b19488b0ee618f5d6346c74281d4@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Stage 33 Live has been running a Local Curator series of shows
  this summer\, turning over the room to local heroes and letting them call
  the shots. The final one in the series belongs to Olivia Nied\, born and 
 bred in Chester\, Vermont. This is a 3:00 matinee on Sunday\, August 9\, 2
 026\, featuring Star Lane Sox and Scott Hsu. <br/><br/>Olivia is half of S
 tar Lane Sox\, a guitar-and-drums indie/punk duo. Influenced by the garage
  rock revival bands of the early 2000s but giving it their own spin\, Star
  Lane Sox formed organically through its two founding members meeting at a
 n open mic. Singer / songwriter / arranger / producer / multi-instrumental
 ist / performer / session musician Olivia was trained at Goldsmiths London
  University\, the Berklee College of Music jazz program\, and the Vermont 
 Jazz Center. She has toured the US\, performed at music festivals in the U
 K\, and played clubs in London\, Paris\, and Amsterdam. Her songs frequent
 ly draw from her lived experience as a neurodivergent\, transgender young 
 person pursuing radical joy against all odds.<br/><br/>Scott Hsu is a seco
 nd-generation Taiwanese-American whose multi-instrumental soul-searching r
 omantic rock / pop blends electronica beats with live looping synthesizers
 \, guitar\, and vocal effects. His lyrics are rooted in authenticity\, and
  gravitate toward love\, nostalgia\, identity\, transformation\, and redem
 ption. Mandarin-English songs and cross-cultural love expressions reflect 
 a unique identity — global\, hybrid\, personal\, ranging from dreamy Chi
 nglish pop/punk to plucky pop Americana.<br/><br/>Tickets are $20 — all 
 proceeds go to the performers — either in advance through stage33live.co
 m\, or at the door as available. Advance tickets guarantee entry. Only 40 
 tickets will be sold. Advance sales will close at midnight the day before 
 the show\, or when 40 tickets are sold.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Southern Vermont
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/star-lane-
 sox-and-scott-hsu-at-stage-33-live-05-07-2026-10-49-55
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twilight On the Tavern Lawn: Planet Zydeco
DTSTART:20260809T180000
DTEND:20260809T200000
DTSTAMP:20260809T173321Z
UID:437eed7bf552838b29a739adf6a2af@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Planet Zydeco brings the irresistible dance music of southwest
  Louisiana to Putney's Twilight on the Tavern Lawn concert series. Hailing
  from New England\, the band delivers authentic zydeco with infectious ene
 rgy\, featuring accordion\, rubboard\, fiddle\, guitar\, bass\, and drums.
  Their lively performances invite audiences of all ages onto the dance flo
 or. Bring a lawn chair or blanket and enjoy an evening of free outdoor mus
 ic. In case of rain\, the concert will move indoors to Next Stage Arts\, 1
 5 Kimball Hill\, Putney.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Location: Southern Vermont
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/twilight-o
 n-the-tavern-lawn-planet-zydeco-09-07-2026-21-52-36
END:VEVENT
